            <ArticleTitle>A CASE OF BRONCHIAL ASTHMA WITH HYPEREOSINOPHILIA WITH EFFECTIVE SAIBOKUTOU THERAPY.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>231-234</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.15036/arerugi.66.231</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 42 year old woman visited on our hospital because of cough, sputum, pruritus and erythema. She showed peripheral blood eosinophilia, high level of FENO, bronchial hyperresponsiveness. Diagnosis of bronchial asthma and atopic dermatitis was made, but she rejected therapy except for Saibokutou, a Kampo herbal medicine. After 1 year, her symptoms and her laboratory data were improved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
